From 569e3990fc19f94bbc26cf5fa039e26e536cdeee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:39:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Choose the best adapter by alignment score also when using an
 index

AdapterIndex ranked candidate adapters by the number of matching bases,
while MultipleAdapters.match_to (used with --no-index and for all
non-anchored adapters) ranks by alignment score (match +1, mismatch -1,
indel -2), the criterion introduced in Cutadapt 4. The two paths could
therefore assign the same read to different adapters: an 11 nt barcode
matching exactly (score 11) lost against a 12 nt barcode matching with one
inserted base (12 matches, score 10). The index also stored the number of
matches in Match.score, so mixed lists of indexed and non-indexed adapters
compared incompatible quantities.

Store the alignment score in the index (computed from the numbers of
errors and matches and the two lengths), rank and detect ambiguity by
score, and stop the multi-length search early based on the score.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TaHntBDKuZJpMAAMenkC44
