--- a/CHANGES.rst
+++ b/CHANGES.rst
@@ -2,6 +2,18 @@
 Changelog
 =========
 
+development version
+-------------------
+
+* When demultiplexing with an index (that is, when multiple anchored adapters
+  are given), the best-matching adapter is now chosen by alignment score, which
+  is the criterion the regular adapter search and ``--no-index`` use.
+  Previously, the index chose the adapter with the highest number of matching
+  bases, which could assign a read to an adapter that matches only with an
+  inserted base instead of to one that matches exactly, and the ``score``
+  recorded for such matches was the number of matches. The set of reads that
+  are considered ambiguous (and therefore not assigned) can change as well.
+
 v5.2 (2025-10-23)
 -----------------
 
